# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Answer two consecutive optional triggers created by one two-card draw effect.
# Forcing: Sign in Blood draws exactly two cards for the opponent, creating exactly two Kederekt Parasite triggers.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or battlefield actions; the human controls every prompt.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Sign in Blood and both optional triggers reduce the opponent from four life to zero.
#   LOSE = A trigger resolves with the wrong decision or the expected life change is absent.
#   TIMEOUT = Either optional prompt cannot submit or the second prompt never becomes actionable.
# Card roles:
#   Kederekt Parasite — creates one optional damage trigger for each opponent draw.
#   Monastery Swiftspear — satisfies the red-permanent condition.
#   Sign in Blood — creates two draws in one resolution and provides a visible life-total outcome check.
#   Forest — preserves a human priority action after the two triggers resolve.
# Protocol path: Targeted cast, two trigger objects, then two ordered OptionalActionMessage/Resp exchanges.

